1
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:09,630
太棒啦 太厉害啦
Bravo! Bravo!

2
00:00:17,590 --> 00:00:19,231
好样的
Bravo!

3
00:00:19,460 --> 00:00:20,341
棒极了
Bravo!

4
00:00:21,960 --> 00:00:24,670
太厉害了 曼尼 厉害
Bravo, Manny! Bravo!

5
00:00:24,670 --> 00:00:26,880
当我听说曼尼想学击剑时 我心想
Well, when I heard Manny wanted to fence, I was, like,

6
00:00:26,880 --> 00:00:29,460
笨手笨脚的孩子 配上致命的利器
"Sure. Uncoordinated kid, lethal weapon.

7
00:00:29,460 --> 00:00:31,100
能有比这还糟的吗
How can this go wrong?"

8
00:00:35,640 --> 00:00:37,460
现在你的看法又如何呢
What do you think now?

9
00:00:38,160 --> 00:00:39,440
我们的小佐罗真让我骄傲
I'm proud of our little Zorro.

10
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:42,140
虽说我也教过他几招 但他的确有天赋
I mean I worked with him a little, but the kid's got skills.

11
00:00:42,220 --> 00:00:46,034
那是与生俱来的 他爹就是个剑术大师
It's in his blood. His father was a master swordsman.

12
00:00:46,034 --> 00:00:48,320
堪称剑道里的艺术家
He was an artist with his sword.

13
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:50,820
他英姿焕发 挥剑抬足的样子
I mean, the way he throws the sword.

14
00:00:50,980 --> 00:00:52,520
他就是传奇
I mean, he was legendary.

15
00:00:52,680 --> 00:00:54,780
你知道我在享受和你儿子的父子时刻吗
You know this nice moment I'm having with your son?

16
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:57,420
-你有点破坏气氛了 -对不起
- You're kind of wrecking it. - Sorry.

17
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:02,395
你们知道剑术起源于12世纪吗
Did you know that fencing goes back to the 12th century?

18
00:01:02,395 --> 00:01:05,280
你知道什么比击剑还呆吗
You know what's even nerdier than fencing?

19
00:01:05,280 --> 00:01:06,380
了解它的起源
Knowing when it began.

20
00:01:06,720 --> 00:01:08,500
我可不认为你是呆子 艾丽克斯
I don't think you're a nerd, Alex.

21
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:09,500
闭嘴吧 呆子
Shut up, dork.

22
00:01:09,860 --> 00:01:11,840
就是这样 乖儿子
All right. That's my boy!

23
00:01:15,100 --> 00:01:16,200
我们不如用起重机帮你
Would this be easier...

24
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:17,480
把这玩意吊起来吧
if we suspended you from a crane?

25
00:01:18,860 --> 00:01:20,600
家庭录像谁都会拍
Any monkey can shoot a home movie.

26
00:01:21,060 --> 00:01:23,440
但只有我能拍出家庭电影的感觉
I pride myself on shooting home films.

27
00:01:23,460 --> 00:01:25,280
但是小卡 你做事总是做得太过了
But, Cameron, you always just take things a little too far.

28
00:01:25,280 --> 00:01:25,736
我才没有
No, I don't.

29
00:01:25,736 --> 00:01:27,760
-你侄子的周岁生日 -说那事儿不公平
- Okay, your nephew's first birthday. - That's not fair.

30
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:29,177
你带了台鼓风机去
You brought a wind machine.

31
00:01:29,177 --> 00:01:30,261
-老实说 -卡梅隆
- To be fair, - Cameron,

32
00:01:30,261 --> 00:01:32,860
-我本来是要 -那可是鼓风机呀
- my vision was- - you brought a wind machine.

33
00:01:32,860 --> 00:01:34,200
谁会在婴儿床上装轮子
Who puts wheels on cribs?

34
00:01:42,842 --> 00:01:44,382
抱歉 抱歉
Ay! Sorry. Sorry.

35
00:01:45,748 --> 00:01:47,031
尽管抱
That's okay.

36
00:01:47,340 --> 00:01:48,880
不不不不 我手机没电了
No. No, no, no, no! My phone died.

37
00:01:49,140 --> 00:01:51,640
没什么 大概是你手机电池没静电了
No biggie. Your battery probably just statically defracticated.

38
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:53,280
什么
What?

39
00:01:53,560 --> 00:01:55,840
你给它充点静电就行了
It means you can recharge it with static electricity.

40
00:01:56,160 --> 00:01:57,560
在你头发上蹭蹭就好了
Just rub it on your hair.

41
00:02:01,220 --> 00:02:01,620
太棒了
Yes!

42
00:02:02,100 --> 00:02:04,220
我以前去朋友家
You know, I used to go to the houses of my friends,

43
00:02:04,320 --> 00:02:05,420
看见他们小孩得的奖杯
I'd see their kids' trophies,

44
00:02:05,580 --> 00:02:07,020
心里都特别不舒服
and it used to bug me, you know,

45
00:02:07,020 --> 00:02:09,240
因为我家从来没得过奖杯
because there was never a trophy in my house.

46
00:02:09,760 --> 00:02:11,000
直到她的出现
Not until this one.

47
00:02:13,015 --> 00:02:15,052
你的手劲真大
Oh, that's a good grip.

48
00:02:18,718 --> 00:02:20,191
和我换换位置吧
Can we switch seats?

49
00:02:21,340 --> 00:02:22,300
小卡 别人在看你呢
Cam, people are staring.

50
00:02:22,860 --> 00:02:24,380
我知道父母不该在意这些事
I know you're not supposed to care,

51
00:02:24,380 --> 00:02:26,400
但是家里有个有特长的孩子
but it's kind of cool to have a kid in your house

52
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:27,420
感觉挺不错的
who's the best at something.

53
00:02:27,420 --> 00:02:28,160
你懂我的意思吧
You know what I mean?

54
00:02:31,940 --> 00:02:34,300
-我家小孩都很棒 -他们是最棒的
- Yeah, our kids are great. - They're the greatest.

55
00:02:34,880 --> 00:02:37,340
-我们真幸运 -没错 不过呢
- Gosh, we're blessed. - We are. But, um,

56
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:39,300
要说他们有什么特长吗
are they the best at something?

57
00:02:40,040 --> 00:02:41,340
我得好好想想
I'd have to think about that.

58
00:02:41,700 --> 00:02:43,800
只要艾丽克斯想做的 她都能做到最好
Well, Alex is great at every single thing she tries,

59
00:02:43,860 --> 00:02:46,660
-所以她总会找到自己的特长 -是的
- so, you know, she'll find her specialty. - She will.

60
00:02:46,840 --> 00:02:47,940
至于海莉嘛
And Haley is-

61
00:02:53,760 --> 00:02:55,760
海莉长得多漂亮啊
Haley is so pretty.

62
00:02:55,886 --> 00:02:58,554
-美若天仙 我女儿美若天仙 -没错
- Gorgeous, gorgeous girl. - Oh, gosh.

63
00:02:58,680 --> 00:03:00,740
所以她可以嫁个有特长的男人
So she can meet someone who's the best at something.

64
00:03:00,820 --> 00:03:01,358
说的对
That's right.

65
00:03:01,358 --> 00:03:03,926
然后 还剩下卢克
And then, uh, I guess that leaves Luke.

66
00:03:08,780 --> 00:03:10,180
他是有点输在起跑线上了
We dropped the ball a little bit on that one.

67
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:10,800
的确 有那么一点
Yeah, a little bit.

68
00:03:24,089 --> 00:03:25,475
厉害
Bravo!

69
00:03:26,420 --> 00:03:30,360
请为我们的胜利者曼尼·迪尔加多鼓掌
How about a nice round of applause for our winner, Manny Delgado.

70
00:03:31,780 --> 00:03:33,700
曼尼晋级了总冠军争夺赛
Manny now moves on to the championship,

71
00:03:33,760 --> 00:03:36,647
他将对阵卡罗琳·马可
where he'll be competing against Caroline Markum.

72
00:03:37,987 --> 00:03:40,111
请在四点半准时到场观看比赛
We'll see you all back here at 4:30.

73
00:03:40,180 --> 00:03:41,480
-太好了 -儿子你真棒
- All right. - Bravo.

74
00:03:46,944 --> 00:03:48,475
我想说的和她一样
What she said.

75
00:03:49,820 --> 00:03:51,640
老爸比曼尼还激动啊
Wow. This means more to Dad than it does to Manny.

76
00:03:51,780 --> 00:03:54,020
是啊 这可是他成为冠军之父的机会
Yeah, it's his chance to be father of a champion.

77
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:55,080
其实 以前也有过机会
Well, second chance.

78
00:03:55,700 --> 00:03:57,460
我们都知道那次是怎么错过了
We all know how the first time went.

79
00:03:58,520 --> 00:03:59,299
我说错什么了吗
Did I say something wrong?

80
00:03:59,299 --> 00:04:02,729
没 才没呢 我只是太为曼尼高兴了
No, no. I'm- I'm very happy for Manny.That's all.

81
00:04:04,132 --> 00:04:06,000
什么事都能扯到她身上 神啊
Everything's always about Claire. Geez.

82
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:08,840
谢谢你们过来支持我儿子
I wanna thank you guys for coming by and supporting the kid.

83
00:04:09,120 --> 00:04:10,040
你们是最棒的家人
You guys are the best!

84
00:04:11,140 --> 00:04:12,100
为什么受伤的总是我 克莱尔
Why, Claire?

85
00:04:14,980 --> 00:04:15,460
不是吧你
Really?

86
00:04:19,880 --> 00:04:20,500
你怎么去了那么久
That took a while.

87
00:04:21,220 --> 00:04:22,420
她20分钟前就睡着了
She's been asleep for 20 minutes.

88
00:04:22,420 --> 00:04:25,480
为了不弄醒她 我不得不悄悄溜走
It just took me some time to sneak out without waking her up.

89
00:04:25,820 --> 00:04:27,220
就像你第一次在这里过夜那样
Kind of like the first time you slept over here.

90
00:04:27,440 --> 00:04:29,040
我那是要溜出去开会
I had a meeting.

91
00:04:29,440 --> 00:04:32,120
好吧 我们来谈谈让你心烦意乱的原因
All right. Let's talk about why you got your panties in a bunch.

92
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:33,880
你和你姐之间到底怎么了
What's up with you and your sister?

93
00:04:34,620 --> 00:04:36,680
-什么都没有 -是吗
- Nothing is up. - Mm-hmm.

94
00:04:37,960 --> 00:04:41,220
是不是和滑冰那事有关呀
Or could this have something to do with... ice skating?

95
00:04:43,220 --> 00:04:44,638
米奇尔和克莱尔小时候
When Mitchell and Claire were kids.

96
00:04:44,638 --> 00:04:45,909
没人想听这个故事
This is interesting to no one.

97
00:04:45,980 --> 00:04:48,080
拜托 让我讲完 谢谢
Excuse, please. Let me finish. Thank you.

98
00:04:48,138 --> 00:04:49,236
-在米奇尔10岁时 -11岁
- When Mitchell was 10 - Eleven.

99
00:04:49,300 --> 00:04:51,220
克莱尔13岁时 他们是
And Claire was 13, they

100
00:04:51,220 --> 00:04:52,980
-一对实力雄厚的冰舞小将 -是花样滑冰
- were competitive ice dancers. - Figure skaters!

101
00:04:53,120 --> 00:04:55,060
算了 还是换我来说吧 是的
Oh, for God's sakes, I'll tell the story. Yes,

102
00:04:55,140 --> 00:04:57,700
我姐和我真心是一对完美搭档
my sister and I were actually a very good team.

103
00:04:58,180 --> 00:04:59,840
我们的组合叫"柔情似火"
We were called "Fire and Nice."

104
00:05:00,380 --> 00:05:04,500
我的红发象征火焰 克莱尔代表柔情
I was Fire, because of the red hair, and Claire was Nice,

105
00:05:04,500 --> 00:05:06,600
那是为了讽刺她一点不温柔
because it was ironic and she wasn't.

106
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:08,200
米奇尔到现在还耿耿于怀
And Mitchell is still upset

107
00:05:08,200 --> 00:05:10,160
因为克莱尔在某场比赛前临阵脱逃了
because Claire quit the team right before some meet.

108
00:05:10,280 --> 00:05:13,500
什么某场 那是13岁以下地区总决赛
"Some meet." The 13-and-under regional championships.

109
00:05:13,700 --> 00:05:16,200
那是我人生黄砖路尽头辉煌的翡翠城
Just the Emerald City at the end of my yellow brick road.

110
00:05:16,440 --> 00:05:18,520
-哇 你成功了 -什么
- Wow. You did it. - What?

111
00:05:18,520 --> 00:05:20,600
成功地把滑冰描述得更基情了
You made figure skating sound even gayer.

112
00:05:23,240 --> 00:05:24,920
看到你老爸那么为曼尼骄傲
So, seeing your dad so proud of Manny...

113
00:05:24,920 --> 00:05:26,340
你都没有不爽吗
didn't stir up any resentment?

114
00:05:26,412 --> 00:05:29,640
-才没有 -好吧
- Mm-mmm. - Oh.

115
00:05:29,772 --> 00:05:31,080
好吧 你总是这样
Okay, fine. You always do this.

116
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:32,979
不断压抑自己的情感
Instead of letting your feelings out, you bury them,

117
00:05:32,979 --> 00:05:35,197
等到某一刻再伤人地爆发
and then they bubble up later in hurtful ways.

118
00:05:35,197 --> 00:05:38,240
好啦 你说对了 听着
Okay, you know what? Yes. All right, listen.

119
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:40,700
我或许仍有些不满
I might still be holding a little resentment,

120
00:05:40,700 --> 00:05:43,840
可那很丢人 又显得心胸狭隘
but that's... embarrassing and petty

121
00:05:43,840 --> 00:05:45,920
我再那样也不合适了
and it's not a good color on me.

122
00:05:46,023 --> 00:05:48,497
就像你不适合黄颜色
It's kind of like you and yellow.

123
00:05:48,600 --> 00:05:50,080
你不是很喜欢我穿黄色衣服吗
You love me in my yellow shirt.

124
00:05:50,144 --> 00:05:52,265
黄色让你看起来像个太阳
It makes you look like the sun.

125
00:05:52,340 --> 00:05:53,440
爆发了 伤人地爆发了
Bubbling. Hurtful bubbling.

126
00:05:54,380 --> 00:05:56,260
现在你知道我那早为何溜走了
Now you know why I left early that morning.

127
00:05:57,080 --> 00:05:59,920
我就知道你不是开会 小卡 我就知道
I knew you didn't have a meeting, Cam. I knew it.

128
00:06:03,980 --> 00:06:05,820
这手机肯定出了什么毛病
There must be something wrong with this phone.

129
00:06:05,860 --> 00:06:07,820
我都在头上蹭一个钟头了
I've rubbed it on my head for, like, an hour.

130
00:06:08,900 --> 00:06:11,180
什么 艾丽克斯
What? Alex.

131
00:06:11,253 --> 00:06:14,017
天啊 你真是个怪胎
Oh, you're such a geek.

132
00:06:14,080 --> 00:06:16,660
至少我没把头皮磨秃
At least I didn't give myself a bald spot.

133
00:06:16,840 --> 00:06:17,920
天啊 妈妈
Oh, my God! Mom!

134
00:06:18,160 --> 00:06:19,239
艾丽克斯 别这么刻薄
Alex, don't be mean.

135
00:06:19,239 --> 00:06:22,199
海莉 你也别那么容易掉入陷阱
Haley, stop making yourself such an easy target.

136
00:06:22,260 --> 00:06:24,560
就是这样 老弟 就是这样
This feels right, buddy. I'm telling you, this feels right.

137
00:06:24,560 --> 00:06:26,680
-你们要去哪 -去创造天才
- What are you guys doing? - Pursuing excellence.

138
00:06:26,780 --> 00:06:29,340
我们帮卢克列了个成功潜力表
We make a list of areas the boy might excel at

139
00:06:29,340 --> 00:06:32,040
-然后选择了棒球 -不错
- and... baseball. - Love it.

140
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:35,080
是啊 书上说一万小时的训练就能练成天才
Yeah. I read it only takes 10,000 hours to achieve excellence.

141
00:06:35,140 --> 00:06:37,740
你已经练了 你大概练多久了
You've already got, what, how many hours playing ball?

142
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:42,120
我练一个赛季了 得有六千小时吧
Well, I played, like, one season, so, like, 6,000 hours?

143
00:06:43,120 --> 00:06:44,980
怪不得你们没选数学
Yeah. I can see why you ruled out math.

144
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:48,480
我当然想要卢克成功
Yeah, of course I want Luke to be successful.

145
00:06:48,560 --> 00:06:51,600
可我不喜欢揠苗助长
But I don't think that a parent can just force that.

146
00:06:52,080 --> 00:06:53,736
我觉得你只要有信心
I think you just have to have

147
00:06:53,736 --> 00:06:57,061
孩子们会发现自己的闪光点
faith that the kid's gonna find his own way.

148
00:06:58,040 --> 00:07:02,440
再说 能成为我儿子 已经够卢克骄傲了
Besides, Luke already is the best at something- being my son.

149
00:07:04,508 --> 00:07:07,942
这话说出口来就弱掉了
It sounded a lot less lame in my head.

150
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:10,160
我预感这将会进展顺利
I have got a good feeling about this.

151
00:07:10,198 --> 00:07:11,242
你肯定是打棒球的料
This is gonna be your sport.

152
00:07:11,280 --> 00:07:14,340
去年你说过我是打篮球的料
Last year, you said basketball was my sport.

153
00:07:14,840 --> 00:07:17,600
听着 我说过很多让我追悔莫及的话
Look, I've said a lot of things I wish I could take back but I can't.

154
00:07:18,140 --> 00:07:19,300
我能做的
What I can do...

155
00:07:19,300 --> 00:07:24,859
只有当一个能够帮助你登上顶峰的爸爸
is be the dad you need me to be to help you become masterful.

156
00:07:24,859 --> 00:07:27,173
-你想登峰造极吗 -大概吧
- You wanna be masterful? - I guess.

157
00:07:27,236 --> 00:07:29,508
真是个好孩子 好吧
There's my killer! Okay.

158
00:07:30,340 --> 00:07:32,860
我们一万小时的训练计划
Our journey of 10,000 hours...

159
00:07:32,860 --> 00:07:34,660
就从简单的投球开始吧
begins with a single pitch.

160
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:37,440
我看好你哟
I believe in my boy.

161
00:07:37,685 --> 00:07:40,243
我不会放弃你的
I ain't gonna quit you.

162
00:07:40,320 --> 00:07:41,660
投一个过来
Let's burn one in here.

163
00:07:42,120 --> 00:07:44,500
很好 你开了一个好头
That's good. That's a good start.

164
00:07:44,987 --> 00:07:50,089
你休息一下 我去捡球
Okay, you rest that cannon while I run this down, okay?

165
00:07:50,165 --> 00:07:53,873
尽量往这个方向投球
Okay, let's keep all the batters right here.

166
00:07:53,949 --> 00:07:57,895
我该把护裆穿上 真该把护裆穿上
Oh, should've- should've worn my cup. Should've worn my cup.

167
00:07:57,960 --> 00:07:58,840
全垒打[打进家里]
Home run!

168
00:07:59,260 --> 00:08:01,200
球肯定在这里的某处 老弟
This one's really in here, buddy.

169
00:08:06,278 --> 00:08:09,918
很好 第一个小时真是非常非常不错
Okay. Very, very, very, very good first hour.

170
00:08:09,980 --> 00:08:12,640
把手套给我 我给它上点油
Toss me your glove. I'll put some oil on it.

171
00:08:26,542 --> 00:08:28,282
-没事吧 -没事
- Everything okay? - Yes.

172
00:08:28,340 --> 00:08:30,980
我刚告诉奶奶 曼尼今天有多厉害
I was telling my grandmother how great was Manny today.

173
00:08:30,980 --> 00:08:32,300
你不是在吵架啊
So that wasn't angry talk?

174
00:08:33,180 --> 00:08:34,320
才不是 傻瓜 我聊得开心呢
No, silly. That was happy talk.

175
00:08:34,760 --> 00:08:35,720
我开始了解
I'm beginning to understand

176
00:08:35,720 --> 00:08:37,720
为啥你们南美那么多暴力冲突了
why there's so much conflict on your continent.

177
00:08:38,380 --> 00:08:39,540
来 看看这个
Here. Check this out.

178
00:08:40,885 --> 00:08:43,418
哦 杰
Ah, Jay.

179
00:08:47,340 --> 00:08:48,820
来吧 宝贝 给他们瞧瞧
Come on, baby. Show them.

180
00:08:48,940 --> 00:08:51,880
几年前 我孙女海莉跑五千米
A few years back, my granddaughter Haley ran a 5K,

181
00:08:51,900 --> 00:08:53,540
于是我做了一些这样的衬衫
so I had a few of these made up.

182
00:08:54,500 --> 00:08:55,320
太好玩了
It's just fun.

183
00:08:58,014 --> 00:09:00,212
我很高兴你那么为曼尼骄傲
I love it when you're so proud of Manny.

184
00:09:00,212 --> 00:09:00,793
确实 老实说
You know, I'm not gonna lie.

185
00:09:00,886 --> 00:09:02,918
看见他把那些小孩打得落花流水
Seeing him out there slicing those kids to pieces,

186
00:09:02,918 --> 00:09:04,587
我真是开心
you know, it gets to ya.

187
00:09:04,587 --> 00:09:08,516
-多谢你 宝贝 -很抱歉打断你们
- Gracias, mi amor. - I'm sorry to interrupt.

188
00:09:08,620 --> 00:09:11,260
-没事 -小冠军 给你点小东西
- It's okay, papi. - Hey, champ! I got a little something for you.

189
00:09:11,340 --> 00:09:13,460
我也正要给你个东西 拿着
And I have something for you. Here.

190
00:09:15,631 --> 00:09:18,136
我不再需要它了
I will not be needing it anymore.

191
00:09:18,220 --> 00:09:20,820
-那决赛怎么办 -我要退役了
- But the finals? - I am retired.

192
00:09:26,700 --> 00:09:27,900
等下 等下 等下
Wait, wait, wait.

193
00:09:28,920 --> 00:09:30,360
你不能退役啊
You can't retire.

194
00:09:31,060 --> 00:09:32,640
我觉得这不好玩了
It's just not fun anymore.

195
00:09:32,640 --> 00:09:34,281
那只是你一时冲动
Well, that's probably just butterflies.

196
00:09:34,483 --> 00:09:36,175
拜托 你没问题的
Come on. You're gonna be fine.

197
00:09:36,336 --> 00:09:39,226
听着 如果他不想比 那是他的决定
Look, if he doesn't want to, it's his decision.

198
00:09:39,226 --> 00:09:40,938
决定个鬼
Ah, the hell it is.

199
00:09:41,160 --> 00:09:43,520
他觉得太紧张 就别逼他做
He shouldn't be doing anything that makes him nervous.

200
00:09:44,220 --> 00:09:45,240
宝贝 我支持你
Papi, I support you.

201
00:09:45,320 --> 00:09:47,840
我不是紧张 我只是不想和一个女孩对决
I'm not nervous. I just don't want to fight a girl.

202
00:09:48,560 --> 00:09:49,020
什么
What?

203
00:09:49,800 --> 00:09:51,940
赢过一个女人会是我荣誉册上的污点
Defeating a woman will be a mark on my honor.

204
00:09:52,020 --> 00:09:52,340
为啥
Why?

205
00:09:52,340 --> 00:09:55,073
因为你们男人总是比我们女人厉害吗
Because men are always so superior to woman?

206
00:09:57,320 --> 00:10:00,760
你厉害得连话都说不全了吗
So superior that you cannot even finish your sentence?

207
00:10:01,920 --> 00:10:02,520
老弟
Dude.

208
00:10:03,660 --> 00:10:07,240
曼尼 你常称自己为女人的贴心小情人
Manny, you always call yourself the lover of women,

209
00:10:07,620 --> 00:10:09,400
如果你不和那女孩比赛
but if you don't compete with this girl,

210
00:10:09,620 --> 00:10:12,920
就说明你根本不尊重我们女人
you're showing me and all the woman that you don't respect us.

211
00:10:14,340 --> 00:10:15,219
对不起
I'm sorry.

212
00:10:15,219 --> 00:10:17,569
所以 拿回你的剑
Okay, so, take back your sword...

213
00:10:17,569 --> 00:10:20,888
-像个公牛一样打败她 -好的
- and go fight this girl like a bull. - Okay.

214
00:10:21,131 --> 00:10:22,922
-说大声点 -好的
- Can't hear you! - Okay!

215
00:10:22,922 --> 00:10:27,011
-再大声点 -那真是我最大嗓门了
- I can't hear you! - That's really as loud as I can go.

216
00:10:28,760 --> 00:10:30,160
如何成为一名好的推销员
What does it take to make a great salesman?

217
00:10:30,280 --> 00:10:31,060
其实没什么窍门
It's no big secret.

218
00:10:31,160 --> 00:10:34,980
只要遵从销售的基本法则 "一定要成交"
You just follow the ABC's of salesmanship: Always Be Closing.

219
00:10:35,180 --> 00:10:35,940
永远不要忘记
Don't ever forget

220
00:10:35,940 --> 00:10:38,540
好的房屋卖点就藏在你身边
great home ideas just keep lurking, mostly nearby.

221
00:10:38,619 --> 00:10:41,372
人们通常会质疑房产经纪人的诚实度
Often people question realtors' sincerity.

222
00:10:41,440 --> 00:10:43,120
你马上装作生气 冒犯者就会
Take umbrage. Violators will-

223
00:10:43,177 --> 00:10:44,793
糟了 什么词是X开头的...
Oh, shoot. X- X-

224
00:10:44,860 --> 00:10:46,560
这间屋子真心棒
And this is the great room,

225
00:10:46,660 --> 00:10:49,660
即使"棒"这个词已经配不上这间屋了
although "Great" hardly seems to do a room like this justice.

226
00:10:50,020 --> 00:10:52,080
请忽略这幅诡异的弯弯曲曲的画
Weird, squiggly painting not included.

227
00:10:52,320 --> 00:10:53,680
-其实我挺喜欢这画的 -我也喜欢
- I actually love it. - I do too.

228
00:10:53,680 --> 00:10:54,723
真美
It's really beautiful.

229
00:10:54,723 --> 00:10:57,332
橱柜都是定制内嵌的 你会发现
Um, all custom built-ins, and you will notice just-

230
00:10:57,380 --> 00:11:00,500
房子采光充足 多好啊
just tons of natural light, so that's great.

231
00:11:00,900 --> 00:11:02,040
我想做成这笔生意吗 当然想
Did I need the sale? Yes.

232
00:11:02,120 --> 00:11:03,300
但我为之担心吗 当然不
Was I worried? No.

233
00:11:03,560 --> 00:11:05,760
为啥 因为 因为啥呢
Why? Because. Because why?

234
00:11:05,900 --> 00:11:09,180
因为我不会推销我不相信的东西
Because I won't sell anything I don't believe in.

235
00:11:09,300 --> 00:11:12,160
当我信了 你也会信的
And when I believe, you believe.

236
00:11:13,264 --> 00:11:15,584
我能把皮毛大衣卖给一个爱斯基摩人
I could sell a fur coat to an Eskimo.

237
00:11:15,651 --> 00:11:18,027
菲尔 很抱歉 这个房子很漂亮
Yeah, Phil, I'm sorry. It's a beautiful house.

238
00:11:18,040 --> 00:11:20,460
只是我不确定这是否适合孩子居住
But I'm just not sure how kid-friendly it is,

239
00:11:20,460 --> 00:11:21,660
我们有两个小孩
and we have two small children.

240
00:11:21,720 --> 00:11:22,781
光是这些楼梯
I mean, these stairs alone.

241
00:11:22,781 --> 00:11:23,783
老爸 这地方酷毙了
Dad, this place is awesome.

242
00:11:23,880 --> 00:11:25,395
-现在不行 卢克 -你看后院了吗
- Not now, Luke. - Did you see the backyard?

243
00:11:25,395 --> 00:11:27,545
足以放下十间树屋呢
It's got room for 10 tree houses.

244
00:11:27,620 --> 00:11:29,820
卧室的天花板上有窗户
And the bedroom's got a window on the ceiling.

245
00:11:30,460 --> 00:11:31,860
我希望我们也能住在这儿
I wish we could live here.

246
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:34,180
-我希望你回露台去 -真的吗
- I wish you'd go back out to the patio where- - Do you really?

247
00:11:35,300 --> 00:11:39,100
是的 我家房子比这差多了
Oh, yeah. Our house sucks compared to this one.

248
00:11:39,820 --> 00:11:41,040
确实差太多
It really does.

249
00:11:45,540 --> 00:11:46,380
你们回来啦
There you are.

250
00:11:46,437 --> 00:11:47,309
我去换衣服
I'm gonna get changed and

251
00:11:47,309 --> 00:11:48,775
然后一起去看曼尼的比赛
then we'll go back to Manny's match, okay?

252
00:11:48,880 --> 00:11:51,760
-爸爸不希望我去 -什么 为什么
- Dad doesn't want me to go. - What? Why?

253
00:11:51,837 --> 00:11:54,233
还记得你曾担心咱儿子很没用吗
Remember when you were all worried that our son's a dud?

254
00:11:54,233 --> 00:11:57,420
我印象中可没说"没用"什么的
Okay. That's not exactly the way I remember it.

255
00:11:57,420 --> 00:11:59,120
实验证明 他很有天分
Turns out he's a natural.

256
00:11:59,940 --> 00:12:01,860
-哪方面 -推销
- At what? - At selling.

257
00:12:03,660 --> 00:12:05,520
住宅房地产的泰坦巨神们
Hey, Titans of residential real estate.

258
00:12:05,800 --> 00:12:06,780
对 哥就说你们呢
That's right, I'm talking to you,

259
00:12:06,780 --> 00:12:10,872
桑迪·布鲁斯特 斯奇普·沃思南 麦卡宾
Sandy Brewster, Skip Woosnum, J.J. McCubbin.

260
00:12:10,940 --> 00:12:13,516
听到后浪的脚步了吗 那是卢克·邓菲
Hear those footsteps? That's Luke Dunphy,

261
00:12:13,516 --> 00:12:16,269
他要把你们拍死在沙滩上了
and he's gonna drink your milk shake.

262
00:12:18,120 --> 00:12:19,160
不可思议
That's amazing.

263
00:12:19,180 --> 00:12:20,480
-对吧 -难以置信
- Right? - Incredible.

264
00:12:20,480 --> 00:12:21,740
然后买家将在一个小时内
So, the buyer's coming back

265
00:12:21,740 --> 00:12:23,680
和她丈夫一起过来 我需要卢克
in an hour with her husband, and I need him.

266
00:12:23,740 --> 00:12:25,880
告诉你 这孩子是个天才
I am telling you, that kid is a genius.

267
00:12:26,260 --> 00:12:27,540
我们的招财小神童驾到
There's the rainmaker.

268
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:31,500
-你的iPod怎么在嘴里 -给它充电呢
- Why is your iPod in your mouth? - I'm charging it.

269
00:12:32,220 --> 00:12:34,080
艾丽克斯 艾丽克斯
Alex. Alex!

270
00:12:39,660 --> 00:12:41,320
难道你一点也不想
So, there's no part of you

271
00:12:41,320 --> 00:12:42,800
和你姐姐消除误会吗
that wants to clear the air with your sister?

272
00:12:43,120 --> 00:12:43,413
不想
Nope.

273
00:12:43,413 --> 00:12:45,934
好吧 我尊重你家的处事方式
Okay, fine. That's your family's way. I'll respect that.

274
00:12:46,020 --> 00:12:48,460
但你该知道 这对爱你的人来说很难受
But you should know, it's hard on the people who love you.

275
00:12:48,565 --> 00:12:49,980
-小卡 -你让我们压力山大
- Cam - We feel the tension.

276
00:12:49,980 --> 00:12:52,460
你说的话句句伤人
We hear the words that cut like knives.

277
00:12:52,540 --> 00:12:55,448
各位 我带了切好的橙子
Hey, guys! I brought orange slices.

278
00:12:55,528 --> 00:12:57,675
好吧 我受不了了
Okay, you know what? I can't bear this.

279
00:12:57,800 --> 00:12:59,100
克莱尔 米奇尔仍然对你小时候
Claire, Mitchell still resents you

280
00:12:59,100 --> 00:13:01,200
退出花样滑冰队的事耿耿于怀
for quitting the figure skating team when you were kids.

281
00:13:01,560 --> 00:13:03,080
小姐们 请跟我进去
Ladies, come inside with me, please.

282
00:13:03,120 --> 00:13:05,200
你俩把问题解决了 我们走
Work it out. Come on.

283
00:13:05,720 --> 00:13:07,840
-谢谢 小卡 -他说的是真的吗
- Thanks, Cam. - Is he serious?

284
00:13:07,900 --> 00:13:10,045
所以你今早才用话攻击我吗
Is that what your little jab was about this morning?

285
00:13:10,045 --> 00:13:11,768
不是 是 好吧 是这么回事
Okay. No. Yes. Okay, yes. Yes.

286
00:13:11,820 --> 00:13:13,240
我想我仍然有点小生气
I guess I'm still a little angry.

287
00:13:13,480 --> 00:13:15,860
但你夺走了我的辉煌时刻 克莱尔
But, you know, you stole my moment, Claire.

288
00:13:16,120 --> 00:13:18,780
-是 21年前 -对你来说无所谓
- Yeah, 21 years ago. - Okay, but it doesn't matter to you...

289
00:13:18,780 --> 00:13:20,060
因为你有你自己的光辉时刻
because you had your own moments.

290
00:13:20,200 --> 00:13:22,200
你是啦啦队队长 参演校园剧
You had cheerleading and high school plays

291
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:23,760
还与球队四分卫搞亲热
and making out with the quarterback.

292
00:13:24,100 --> 00:13:25,260
拜托 你也和他搞过
Oh come on, You made out with him too.

293
00:13:25,300 --> 00:13:27,280
是 但我们是偷偷摸摸的
Yeah, but we had to keep it a secret.

294
00:13:29,120 --> 00:13:30,008
你不该退出
You shouldn't have quit.

295
00:13:30,008 --> 00:13:32,181
-太自私了 -想知道我退出的原因吗
- It was selfish. - You wanna know why I quit?

296
00:13:32,300 --> 00:13:35,120
-为了保护你 -保护什么
- I quit to protect you. - From what?

297
00:13:35,235 --> 00:13:36,934
得到荣誉 名声还是记者招待会
Glory? Fame? Press conferences?

298
00:13:36,934 --> 00:13:38,987
别这样 我那时比你重
What? Come on. I was bigger than you.

299
00:13:39,060 --> 00:13:39,880
我比你重
I was bigger than you,

300
00:13:39,940 --> 00:13:41,520
我害怕你举不动我
and I was afraid you wouldn't be able to lift me.

301
00:13:41,640 --> 00:13:43,179
练习的时候你摔了我
You were dropping me in practice,

302
00:13:43,179 --> 00:13:45,353
-我不想让你 -就摔过两次
- And I didn't want you to - I dropped you twice.

303
00:13:45,353 --> 00:13:47,200
-三次 -在那么多人面前丢脸
- Three times. - humiliate yourself in front of all those people.

304
00:13:47,200 --> 00:13:48,500
我一直被你摔
You dropped me all the time.

305
00:13:51,140 --> 00:13:55,980
行啦 你就原谅我 忘掉过去吧
Come on. Could you just forgive me and move on?

306
00:13:57,440 --> 00:14:00,760
当然可以 没错 对不起
Of course. Yes, yes. Yes, of- I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

307
00:14:00,828 --> 00:14:04,232
我是不是很小气
Oh. This must seem so petty, huh?

308
00:14:04,300 --> 00:14:07,000
只是有点傻 但我们都有些小心结 不是吗
Well, it's a little silly, but we all have our thing, don't we?

309
00:14:07,260 --> 00:14:09,360
很高兴你能释怀了
I'm just glad you're getting it out of you.

310
00:14:10,080 --> 00:14:14,040
你是在举我吗 你真的是想把我举起来
Are you trying to lift me? You are. You're trying to lift me. Oh!

311
00:14:19,680 --> 00:14:22,400
保持专注 保持冷静 保持怒气
Stay focused, stay loose and stay angry.

312
00:14:23,380 --> 00:14:25,680
-谁最强悍 -我
- Who's the toughest? - I am.

313
00:14:26,420 --> 00:14:29,340
-谁最勇敢 -我
- Who's the bravest? - I am.

314
00:14:29,620 --> 00:14:30,520
谁最棒
Who's the baddest?

315
00:14:31,600 --> 00:14:33,460
你们能一口气问完吗
Can you guys ask all the questions now

316
00:14:33,460 --> 00:14:34,679
我就不用一遍遍举起这面罩了
so I don't have to keep lifting this?

317
00:14:34,679 --> 00:14:37,146
-上吧 -加油
- Go. - Go get 'em!

318
00:14:37,261 --> 00:14:39,298
-开始了 准备好了吗 -是的
- There we go. You all set? - Yeah.

319
00:14:39,361 --> 00:14:41,881
好嘞 加油 好运哦
Okay, go get 'em. Good luck.

320
00:14:41,996 --> 00:14:44,337
-请问这有人坐吗 -没有 坐吧
- Excuse me. Is this seat taken? - No. Sit.

321
00:14:44,400 --> 00:14:45,120
谢谢
Oh, thank you.

322
00:14:46,300 --> 00:14:48,860
-曼尼是你家孩子吗 -是的
- Oh, is Manny yours? - Yes.

323
00:14:49,260 --> 00:14:50,900
他非常棒 我看过他比赛
Oh, he's quite good. I saw him earlier.

324
00:14:51,320 --> 00:14:51,900
谢谢
Thank you.

325
00:14:52,047 --> 00:14:55,171
-那是你女儿吗 -卡罗琳吗 不是
- Is she your little girl? - Oh, Caroline? No. No.

326
00:14:55,260 --> 00:14:56,920
很遗憾 她的父母都过世了
Sadly, her parents passed away.

327
00:14:57,460 --> 00:14:59,360
我是她在儿童医院的护士
I'm her nurse down at the children's hospital.

328
00:15:00,080 --> 00:15:02,780
但我视所有病人为家人
But all of my patients are like family to me.

329
00:15:08,700 --> 00:15:10,660
孩子们玩得很开心
Well, our boys are enjoying themselves.

330
00:15:10,920 --> 00:15:12,980
是啊 我可以谈论
Yeah. I can talk about

331
00:15:12,980 --> 00:15:15,820
一整天的天花线和嵌入灯
crown moldings and recessed lighting until the cows come home,

332
00:15:15,820 --> 00:15:18,160
但没有什么能与孩子的笑声相媲美
but nothing compares with that sound right there.

333
00:15:19,180 --> 00:15:23,200
老弟啊 他没事
Oh. Hey, buddy. Oh, he's fine.

334
00:15:23,340 --> 00:15:25,038
我的脚 我感觉脚扭过去了
My foot. I think it's backwards.

335
00:15:25,038 --> 00:15:27,340
-没扭过去 -怎么回事
- It's not backwards. - Wh-What happened?

336
00:15:27,340 --> 00:15:29,720
都是这破地板 太滑了
It's the stupid floors! They're too slippery.

337
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:31,940
橡木家具也被称为自然的枕头
Oak. Also known as nature's pillow.

338
00:15:32,240 --> 00:15:35,780
-像冰一样滑 -好了 别责备地板了
- It's like ice. - Now, let's not start blaming the floors.

339
00:15:35,820 --> 00:15:38,260
-你不该跑的 -我看到一个鬼
- You shouldn't have been running. - I saw a ghost.

340
00:15:38,578 --> 00:15:43,920
鬼 我是菲尔·邓菲 是我的错
Ghosts. Hey, Phil Dunphy. Okay, that's me.

341
00:15:43,920 --> 00:15:46,137
这楼梯就像个天然鞋拔子
That's acting like a natural shoehorn.

342
00:15:46,137 --> 00:15:48,280
好吧 大家最好都脱了鞋
Okay. Probably better all take

343
00:15:48,280 --> 00:15:50,760
再上楼参观 跟我来
our shoes off for this part of the tour. Follow me.

344
00:15:51,580 --> 00:15:52,720
她是我们的奇迹
She's our little miracle.

345
00:15:53,640 --> 00:15:55,820
要是她爸爸没死在阿富汗战场
Oh. I only wish her father had made it back

346
00:15:55,820 --> 00:15:57,700
还能来看比赛就好了
from Afghanistan to see this.

347
00:16:00,160 --> 00:16:01,820
我们的啦啦队来了
Oh, there's our cheering section.

348
00:16:01,840 --> 00:16:02,660
这边 朋友们
Over here, you guys.

349
00:16:08,620 --> 00:16:10,940
我的神呐 我们必须阻止他
Oh, my God. We have to stop him.

350
00:16:18,860 --> 00:16:20,480
也许我可以拉响火警警报器
Maybe I can pull the fire alarm.

351
00:16:22,220 --> 00:16:23,600
别指望我会手软
Expect no mercy.

352
00:16:24,780 --> 00:16:25,880
放马过来吧 小子
Bring it on, big boy.

353
00:16:28,968 --> 00:16:31,571
我很高兴爸爸为曼尼骄傲 真的
I'm-I'm glad Dad's proud of Manny. I am.

354
00:16:31,640 --> 00:16:35,660
我只是希望看到他为我们骄傲
I just- It would have been nice to see him that proud of us.

355
00:16:37,160 --> 00:16:38,940
我说我们 其实是指我自己
By us, I mean me.

356
00:16:39,920 --> 00:16:42,920
你真觉得通过花样滑冰
And you sincerely thought that the path to Dad's approval...

357
00:16:42,920 --> 00:16:44,520
能得到爸爸的认可吗
was going to be through figure skating?

358
00:16:44,940 --> 00:16:48,100
米奇尔 我绝对确信爸爸最骄傲的时刻
Mitchell, I am fairly confident that Dad's proudest moment...

359
00:16:48,100 --> 00:16:50,460
是你终于脱下那红色火焰紧身衣之时
was when you finally took off the flame-red unitard.

360
00:16:50,580 --> 00:16:53,120
我又没说我的话一定合理
I am not claiming that any of this is rational.

361
00:16:55,644 --> 00:16:59,553
对不起 我不该这么惹人厌
I'm-I'm sorry. I'm sorry for being such a pill, okay?

362
00:17:00,826 --> 00:17:05,242
其实 我一直为退出而内疚
Um, actually, I always felt very guilty for quitting.

363
00:17:05,314 --> 00:17:07,404
我知道你非常热爱花样滑冰
I know how much you loved figure skating.

364
00:17:08,500 --> 00:17:10,520
我从未真正喜爱过滑冰
I never really loved skating.

365
00:17:11,591 --> 00:17:13,711
什么
Uh, what?

366
00:17:13,777 --> 00:17:16,717
好吧 这么说感觉有点娘
Um, all right, this is gonna sound a little gay.

367
00:17:16,794 --> 00:17:20,094
但是 当我们一起滑冰的时候
But, um, when-when you and I skated together,

368
00:17:20,160 --> 00:17:21,800
你不再是刻薄的姐姐
you weren't the mean older sister

369
00:17:21,800 --> 00:17:23,680
我也不是缠人的小弟弟
and I wasn't the clingy little brother.

370
00:17:23,680 --> 00:17:25,264
我们是一个团队
We were- we were a team, and-

371
00:17:25,790 --> 00:17:26,460
说实在的
Well, let's face it,

372
00:17:26,460 --> 00:17:28,480
过去几年 我们之间渐渐疏远
we've kind of grown apart in the past few years.

373
00:17:28,540 --> 00:17:31,740
因为爸妈的离婚 我们又站在对立面
And with Mom and Dad's divorce, we were on opposing sides.

374
00:17:31,820 --> 00:17:35,380
我只是怀念你我并肩作战的时候
And I- I just- I miss being on your team.

375
00:17:40,948 --> 00:17:43,078
这...
That's...

376
00:17:45,957 --> 00:17:48,793
-是有点娘 -看吧
- a little gay. - There we go.

377
00:17:52,600 --> 00:17:53,160
克莱尔 你要去哪
Claire, where are you going?

378
00:17:54,560 --> 00:17:54,960
克莱尔
Claire?

379
00:17:57,690 --> 00:17:58,480
不是吧
No way.

380
00:17:58,980 --> 00:17:59,680
起来
Get up.

381
00:18:00,244 --> 00:18:01,201
-真的吗 -嗯
- Really? -Mm-m

382
00:18:06,400 --> 00:18:08,680
别把我摔了
Don't drop me.

383
00:18:20,640 --> 00:18:23,540
再不拿开 我给你砸了
Put it away or lose it.

384
00:18:29,580 --> 00:18:31,560
神呐 让这一切停止吧
Somebody's got to put a stop to this.

385
00:18:36,500 --> 00:18:37,780
做得好 米奇尔
That's it, Mitchell.

386
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:50,660
我们能请你们吃冰淇林吗
So, can we take you and Caroline out for ice cream?

387
00:18:51,200 --> 00:18:53,660
不行啊 她有糖尿病
We can't. She's diabetic.

388
00:18:54,120 --> 00:18:55,380
猜都猜到了
Of course she is.

389
00:18:55,493 --> 00:18:58,066
掌声祝贺我们的冠军 曼尼·迪尔加多
A round of applause for our winner, Manny Delgado.

390
00:19:00,380 --> 00:19:02,840
快走吧 把这玩意放后备箱里
Let's get out of here. Get this thing in the trunk.

391
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:05,980
我都不知道我是骄傲还是窘迫了
I can't decide if I'm feeling more proud or mortified.

392
00:19:08,096 --> 00:19:10,399
那现在呢
How about now?

393
00:19:19,040 --> 00:19:21,200
我们教育孩子们说 输赢无所谓
We tell our kids it doesn't matter if you win or lose,

394
00:19:21,340 --> 00:19:22,320
但平心而论
but let's be honest.

395
00:19:24,120 --> 00:19:25,880
胜利的感觉好极了
Winning feels pretty great.

396
00:19:27,340 --> 00:19:30,160
他们在阳光下的那一刻是无与伦比的美丽
There's nothing like that golden moment in the sun.

397
00:19:32,300 --> 00:19:35,960
也许每位家长都希望孩子能有这样的时刻
I think every parent probably wants that for their child.

398
00:19:37,340 --> 00:19:39,800
甚至希望自己也能这样
And maybe a little bit for ourselves too.

399
00:19:42,160 --> 00:19:44,340
有时我们太苛求结果
Sometimes we push too hard.

400
00:19:44,580 --> 00:19:47,763
结果导致许多怨恨和愧疚
And that leads to a lot of resentment and guilt.

401
00:19:47,763 --> 00:19:49,120
太棒了
Yes! Yes!

402
00:19:49,180 --> 00:19:53,340
怎么才不算过分呢 我的想法是
So, how much is too much? Here's where I come out.

403
00:19:53,980 --> 00:19:54,560
愧疚总会过去
Guilt fades.

404
00:19:56,180 --> 00:19:57,860
奖牌才是硬道理
Hardware is forever.

405
00:20:08,260 --> 00:20:10,180
-你在生气 是吗 -没有
- You're mad, aren't you? - I'm not mad.

406
00:20:10,200 --> 00:20:11,620
-是的 你在生气 -我没生气
- Yes, you are. - No, I'm not.

407
00:20:11,840 --> 00:20:14,800
-你有点嫉妒 -我为你俩感到高兴
- You're a little jealous. - I'm happy for the two of you.

408
00:20:15,900 --> 00:20:17,740
好吧 我们也来一次 站在那
All right, come on. We'll do one. Stay there.

409
00:20:18,040 --> 00:20:18,920
-真来呀 -当然
- For real? -Yep.

410
00:20:29,544 --> 00:20:32,030
-感觉好点了吗 -是 我来一次
- Feel better? - Yeah. Oh, do me now. Come on.

411
00:20:32,100 --> 00:20:32,880
开什么国际玩笑
What are you talking about?

412
00:20:34,820 --> 00:20:35,400
你当真
Are you serious?

413
00:20:36,940 --> 00:20:37,520
小卡 别
Cam, no.
